---
layout: null
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>GAIA — Self-Learning Platform for Disease Research</title>
<meta name="description" content="A self-learning platform for computational disease research. Scans genomes, scans the web, and builds knowledge that grows.">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/style.css">
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
    <svg class="hero-bg" viewBox="0 0 1800 900" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice">
        <defs>
            <linearGradient id="helixGrad" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="100%" y2="0%">
                <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#a7f3d0" stop-opacity="0.7"/>
                <stop offset="33%" stop-color="#4ade80" stop-opacity="0.7"/>
                <stop offset="66%" stop-color="#34d399" stop-opacity="0.7"/>
                <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#60a5fa" stop-opacity="0.7"/>
            </linearGradient>
            <radialGradient id="cellGlow" cx="50%" cy="50%" r="50%">
                <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#4ade80" stop-opacity="0.3"/>
                <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#4ade80" stop-opacity="0"/>
            </radialGradient>
        </defs>
        <circle class="cell-pulse" cx="200" cy="150" r="80" fill="url(#cellGlow)"/>
        <circle class="cell-pulse" cx="1600" cy="700" r="120" fill="url(#cellGlow)"/>
        <circle class="cell-pulse" cx="1200" cy="200" r="60" fill="url(#cellGlow)"/>
        <g class="vine-sway" opacity="0.4">
            <path d="M100,900 Q150,700 80,500 Q140,300 100,100" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"/>
        </g>
        <g class="vine-sway" opacity="0.35">
            <path d="M1700,900 Q1650,700 1720,500 Q1660,300 1700,100" stroke="#34d399" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"/>
        </g>
        <g class="helix-flow" transform="translate(900, 450)">
            <path d="M-1200,0 Q-600,-220 0,0 T1200,0" stroke="url(#helixGrad)" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none"/>
            <path d="M-1200,0 Q-600,220 0,0 T1200,0" stroke="url(#helixGrad)" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none"/>
        </g>
        <g>
            <circle class="particle" cx="200" cy="200" r="3" fill="#4ade80"/>
            <circle class="particle" cx="500" cy="680" r="2.5" fill="#a7f3d0"/>
            <circle class="particle" cx="1400" cy="180" r="3" fill="#34d399"/>
            <circle class="particle" cx="1650" cy="580" r="2.5" fill="#60a5fa"/>
            <circle class="particle" cx="900" cy="100" r="3" fill="#4ade80"/>
            <circle class="particle" cx="300" cy="500" r="2.5" fill="#a7f3d0"/>
            <circle class="particle" cx="1500" cy="420" r="3" fill="#4ade80"/>
            <circle class="particle" cx="700" cy="780" r="2.5" fill="#60a5fa"/>
        </g>
            <text class="float-label" x="150" y="120" style="font-family: monospace; font-size: 11px; fill: #4ade80; opacity: 0.25;">ATCG</text>
        <text class="float-label" x="1450" y="180" style="font-family: monospace; font-size: 10px; fill: #60a5fa; opacity: 0.2;">exon</text>
        <text class="float-label" x="350" y="620" style="font-family: monospace; font-size: 10px; fill: #a7f3d0; opacity: 0.2;">intron</text>
        <text class="float-label" x="1250" y="720" style="font-family: monospace; font-size: 11px; fill: #34d399; opacity: 0.25;">GC 0.62</text>
        <text class="float-label" x="750" y="780" style="font-family: monospace; font-size: 10px; fill: #4ade80; opacity: 0.2;">D = 1.16</text>
        <text class="float-label" x="1050" y="140" style="font-family: monospace; font-size: 10px; fill: #60a5fa; opacity: 0.2;">chr6</text>
        <text class="float-label" x="550" y="200" style="font-family: monospace; font-size: 9px; fill: #a7f3d0; opacity: 0.2;">HLA-B</text>
        <text class="float-label" x="1600" y="500" style="font-family: monospace; font-size: 10px; fill: #34d399; opacity: 0.2;">variant</text>
        <text class="float-label" x="250" y="400" style="font-family: monospace; font-size: 9px; fill: #4ade80; opacity: 0.2;">fractal</text>
</svg>

    <div class="eq-layer" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="eq small"  style="top: 8%;  left: 5%;">
            H <span class="op">=</span> <span class="op">−</span> Σ <span class="v">p</span><sub>i</sub> <span class="f">log</span><sub>2</sub> <span class="v">p</span><sub>i</sub>
        </span>
        <span class="eq med"    style="top: 15%; left: 72%;">
            D <span class="op">=</span> <span class="f">lim</span><sub>ε→0</sub> <span class="f">log</span> N(ε) <span class="op">/</span> <span class="f">log</span>(1/ε)
        </span>
        <span class="eq small"  style="top: 22%; left: 30%;">
            E <span class="op">~</span> c · n<sup><span class="v">H</span></sup>
        </span>
        <span class="eq"        style="top: 30%; left: 82%;">
            <span class="v">P</span>(c | x)
        </span>
        <span class="eq med"    style="top: 38%; left: 8%;">
            E <span class="op">=</span> 4ε[ (σ/r)<sup><span class="n">12</span></sup> <span class="op">−</span> (σ/r)<sup><span class="n">6</span></sup> ]
        </span>
        <span class="eq small"  style="top: 44%; left: 60%;">
            w<sub>t+1</sub> <span class="op">=</span> w<sub>t</sub> <span class="op">−</span> η ∇L(w<sub>t</sub>)
        </span>
        <span class="eq large"  style="top: 52%; left: 20%;">
            <span class="v">F</span><sub>1</sub> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="n">2</span> · P · R <span class="op">/</span> (P + R)
        </span>
        <span class="eq med"    style="top: 60%; left: 78%;">
            E <span class="op">=</span> <span class="n">332</span> · q<sub>i</sub> q<sub>j</sub> · e<sup>−κr</sup> <span class="op">/</span> r
        </span>
        <span class="eq small"  style="top: 68%; left: 4%;">
            χ<sub>i</sub> <span class="op">←</span> χ<sub>i</sub> <span class="op">+</span> η q<sub>i</sub> <span class="op">+</span> Σ γ<sub>ij</sub> q<sub>j</sub>
        </span>
        <span class="eq"        style="top: 76%; left: 55%;">
            ΔG <span class="op">=</span> ⟨G⟩<sub>bound</sub> <span class="op">−</span> ⟨G⟩<sub>free</sub>
        </span>
        <span class="eq small"  style="top: 84%; left: 28%;">
            λ ∈ [<span class="n">0</span>, <span class="n">1</span>]
        </span>
        <span class="eq med"    style="top: 90%; left: 74%;">
            ∂E/∂t <span class="op">→</span> <span class="n">0</span>
        </span>
        <span class="eq small"  style="top: 12%; left: 45%;">
            ∫ p(x) dx <span class="op">=</span> <span class="n">1</span>
        </span>
        <span class="eq"        style="top: 65%; left: 40%;">
            <span class="op">∇</span>·F <span class="op">=</span> <span class="n">0</span>
        </span>
        <span class="eq small"  style="top: 48%; left: 88%;">
            Σ<sub>i</sub> q<sub>i</sub> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="n">0</span>
        </span>
        <span class="eq med"    style="top: 3%; left: 55%;">
            ⟨S⟩ <span class="op">=</span> <span class="op">−</span>k<sub>B</sub> Σ p<sub>i</sub> ln p<sub>i</sub>
        </span>
    </div>

    <div class="container hero-content">
        <svg class="hero-logo" width="90" height="90" viewBox="0 0 80 80">
            <defs>
                <linearGradient id="logoGrad" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="100%" y2="100%">
                    <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#a7f3d0"/>
                    <stop offset="50%" stop-color="#4ade80"/>
                    <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#34d399"/>
                </linearGradient>
            </defs>
            <circle class="ring" cx="40" cy="40" r="36" fill="none" stroke="url(#logoGrad)" stroke-width="2"/>
            <path d="M22,40 Q40,18 58,40 T22,40" fill="none" stroke="url(#logoGrad)" stroke-width="2"/>
            <path d="M22,40 Q40,62 58,40 T22,40" fill="none" stroke="url(#logoGrad)" stroke-width="2"/>
            <circle cx="40" cy="40" r="4" fill="#4ade80"/>
        </svg>

        <h1>GAIA</h1>
        <p class="tagline">
            A <strong>self-learning</strong> platform for disease research.
            It reads the genome, reads the web, and grows into something
            that knows more tomorrow than it did today.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-cta">
            <a href="#learning" class="btn btn-primary">How it learns →</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/ObviousSatire/GaiaAI" class="btn">View source</a>
        </div>

        <div class="stats">
            <div class="stat">
                <div class="num static">1.08B</div>
                <div class="label">Variants mapped</div>
            </div>
            <div class="stat">
                <div class="num" data-count="25000000" data-format="m">0</div>
                <div class="label">Compounds indexed</div>
            </div>
            <div class="stat">
                <div class="num" data-count="500" data-format="plus">0</div>
                <div class="label">Curated sources</div>
            </div>
            <div class="stat">
                <div class="num" data-count="1" data-format="tb">0</div>
                <div class="label">Knowledge base</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<section>
    <div class="container-narrow">
        <svg class="divider-leaf" width="40" height="40" viewBox="0 0 40 40">
            <path d="M20,4 Q32,12 20,20 Q8,12 20,4 Z" fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.7"/>
            <path d="M20,20 Q32,28 20,36 Q8,28 20,20 Z" fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.7"/>
        </svg>
        <h2>What <span class="accent">GAIA</span> is</h2>
        <p class="lead">
            A system that reads the genome and reads the web. It discovers
            patterns, grows a knowledge graph, and improves continuously as
            new data arrives — from files, from databases, and from hundreds
            of curated reputable sources.
        </p>
        <p style="color: var(--fg-dim); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.8;">
            Most drug discovery starts with a hypothesis and tests it. GAIA
            starts with the raw genome and the raw literature, and works
            backward. Nothing is hand-coded. The system discovers its own
            patterns.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="capabilities">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>What it does, <span class="accent">end to end</span></h2>
        <div class="cap-grid">
            <div class="cap-item"><h4>Genome scanning</h4><p>Every window of a chromosome classified by its structural signature. Coding regions, conserved patterns, regulatory signals — all identified from raw sequence.</p></div>
            <div class="cap-item"><h4>Variant mapping</h4><p>Population variation placed in context. Each variant tied to gene, pathway, and any known associations. The base layer of the knowledge graph.</p></div>
            <div class="cap-item"><h4>Knowledge graph</h4><p>A growing network of variants, genes, pathways, diseases, and compounds. Every new source adds edges. The graph learns as the field publishes.</p></div>
            <div class="cap-item"><h4>Compound libraries</h4><p>Multiple curated libraries of small molecules and natural products. Thousands upon thousands of candidates ready to be screened against any target.</p></div>
            <div class="cap-item"><h4>Interaction scoring</h4><p>Multiple scoring approaches combined into one ranking. Physical, chemical, and contextual evidence rolled into a single number.</p></div>
            <div class="cap-item"><h4>Protocol design</h4><p>Simulated multi-compound protocols across time. Predicted outcomes, risks, and safety margins — all in one plan.</p></div>
            <div class="cap-item"><h4>Link prediction</h4><p>A trained classifier that predicts missing links in the graph. Improves automatically as the graph grows.</p></div>
            <div class="cap-item"><h4>Open datasets</h4><p>Every stage archived publicly with permanent identifiers. The full pipeline, reproducible from raw public sources.</p></div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <style>
/* ===== base ===== */
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body {
    margin: 0;
    background: #0a0f1a;
    color: #e2e8f0;
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.5;
}
.container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
section { padding: 96px 0; }
h2 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem); margin: 0 0 16px; font-weight: 600; }
h3 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 0 0 12px; font-weight: 600; }
p { margin: 0 0 16px; }
ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; }
li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
.accent { color: #4ade80; }
.lead { font-size: 1.05rem; color: #94a3b8; max-width: 720px; margin-bottom: 32px; }

/* ===== capabilities grid ===== */
.cap-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 24px 36px;
    margin-top: 28px;
}
.cap-item h4 { font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0 0 6px; color: #a7f3d0; font-weight: 600; }
.cap-item p { font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; color: #94a3b8; margin: 0; }

/* ===== learning loops ===== */
.learn-stage {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.3fr;
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 72px;
}
.learn-stage:nth-child(even) { direction: rtl; }
.learn-stage:nth-child(even) > * { direction: ltr; }
.stage-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: monospace; font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em; color: #4ade80;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
}

/* ===== DNA helix (Loop 01) ===== */
.helix-wrap {
    position: relative;
    width: 220px; height: 360px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    perspective: 900px;
}
.helix {
    position: relative; width: 100%; height: 100%;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;
    animation: spin 9s linear infinite;
}
@keyframes spin { from { transform: rotateY(0deg); } to { transform: rotateY(360deg); } }
.rung {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%; width: 120px; height: 6px;
    margin-left: -60px; border-radius: 3px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg,#a7f3d0,#4ade80,#34d399);
    box-shadow: 0 0 12px rgba(74,222,128,0.5);
}
.rung:nth-child(1)  { top: 0;    transform: rotateY(0deg); }
.rung:nth-child(2)  { top: 22px; transform: rotateY(20deg); }
.rung:nth-child(3)  { top: 44px; transform: rotateY(40deg); }
.rung:nth-child(4)  { top: 66px; transform: rotateY(60deg); }
.rung:nth-child(5)  { top: 88px; transform: rotateY(80deg); }
.rung:nth-child(6)  { top: 110px;transform: rotateY(100deg); }
.rung:nth-child(7)  { top: 132px;transform: rotateY(120deg); }
.rung:nth-child(8)  { top: 154px;transform: rotateY(140deg); }
.rung:nth-child(9)  { top: 176px;transform: rotateY(160deg); }
.rung:nth-child(10) { top: 198px;transform: rotateY(180deg); }
.rung:nth-child(11) { top: 220px;transform: rotateY(200deg); }
.rung:nth-child(12) { top: 242px;transform: rotateY(220deg); }
.rung:nth-child(13) { top: 264px;transform: rotateY(240deg); }
.rung:nth-child(14) { top: 286px;transform: rotateY(260deg); }
.rung:nth-child(15) { top: 308px;transform: rotateY(280deg); }
.rung:nth-child(16) { top: 330px;transform: rotateY(300deg); }
.rung:nth-child(17) { top: 352px;transform: rotateY(320deg); }
.scan-sweep {
    position: absolute; left: -20px; right: -20px; height: 3px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg,transparent,#4ade80,transparent);
    box-shadow: 0 0 18px #4ade80;
    animation: sweep 3s ease-in-out infinite;
}
@keyframes sweep { 0%,100% { top: 0; } 50% { top: 100%; } }

/* ===== pipeline vine ===== */
.vine-wrap { position: relative; margin: 48px 0 40px; }
.vine { width: 100%; height: 120px; display: block; }
.vine-nodes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
    margin-top: -12px;
}
.vine-node { text-align: center; }
.vn-num {
    font-family: monospace; font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em; color: #4ade80;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
}
.vn-title { font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 600; color: #e2e8f0; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.vn-desc { font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #94a3b8; }

.sample-out { margin-top: 56px; }
.sample-label {
    font-family: monospace; font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #64748b; margin-bottom: 16px;
}
.sample-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
.sample-table th, .sample-table td {
    padding: 12px 10px; text-align: left;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(148,163,184,0.12);
    color: #94a3b8;
}
.sample-table th {
    color: #64748b; font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 0.75rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;
}
.sample-table td:nth-child(3) { font-family: monospace; color: #a7f3d0; }
.sample-foot { margin-top: 20px; font-size: 0.85rem; color: #64748b; font-style: italic; }

/* ===== math ===== */
.math-narrative { max-width: 780px; margin: 0 auto; }
.math-narrative h3 { margin-top: 48px; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 1.4rem; }
.math-narrative p { color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 24px; }
.equation-stack { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; margin: 28px 0 44px; }
.equation-row {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 90px 1fr 220px;
    align-items: baseline; gap: 20px; padding: 14px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(148,163,184,0.12);
}
.equation-label {
    font-family: monospace; font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em; color: #64748b;
}
.equation-body { font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; font-style: italic; font-size: 1.15rem; color: #e2e8f0; }
.equation-note { font-size: 0.8rem; color: #94a3b8; text-align: right; }
.feature-ribbon { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; margin-top: 8px; }
.feature-ribbon span {
    padding: 8px 16px; border: 1px solid rgba(74,222,128,0.25);
    border-radius: 999px; font-size: 0.85rem; color: #a7f3d0;
    background: rgba(74,222,128,0.05);
}
.math-close { margin-top: 40px; font-style: italic; color: #a7f3d0; }

/* ===== evidence eco layers ===== */
.eco-layers {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; margin-top: 48px;
}
.eco-layer {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 90px 1fr;
    gap: 32px;
    padding: 36px 32px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(148,163,184,0.12);
    border-radius: 14px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: rgba(15,23,42,0.35);
}
.eco-glow {
    position: absolute;
    top: -40%; left: -10%;
    width: 60%; height: 180%;
    filter: blur(60px);
    opacity: 0.18;
    pointer-events: none;
    animation: ecoDrift 16s ease-in-out infinite alternate;
}
.eco-glow-green { background: radial-gradient(circle, #4ade80, transparent 70%); }
.eco-glow-blue  { background: radial-gradient(circle, #60a5fa, transparent 70%); animation-delay: 4s; }
.eco-glow-mint  { background: radial-gradient(circle, #a7f3d0, transparent 70%); animation-delay: 8s; }
@keyframes ecoDrift {
    from { transform: translate3d(0,0,0) scale(1); }
    to   { transform: translate3d(30px,-20px,0) scale(1.15); }
}
.eco-icon { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
.eco-body { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
.eco-tag {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: monospace; font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #4ade80; margin-bottom: 10px;
}
.eco-body h3 { font-size: 1.15rem; color: #e2e8f0; margin: 0 0 10px; }
.eco-body p { font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #94a3b8; margin-bottom: 14px; }
.eco-body ul {
    list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 8px 24px;
}
.eco-body li { font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.6; color: #64748b; }
.eco-body li strong { color: #a7f3d0; font-weight: 600; }

/* ===== cross-cutting validation ===== */
.cross-cut { margin-top: 56px; }
.cross-cut h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; color: #e2e8f0; margin-bottom: 20px; }
.cross-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: 20px 32px;
}
.cross-grid div { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; }
.cross-grid strong { font-size: 0.9rem; color: #a7f3d0; font-weight: 600; }
.cross-grid span { font-size: 0.82rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.55; }

/* ===== sources / reading strip ===== */
.source-hero { margin-top: 48px; }
.source-hero-label {
    font-family: monospace; font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #4ade80; margin-bottom: 14px;
}
.source-hero h3 { font-size: 1.35rem; color: #e2e8f0; margin: 0 0 14px; }
.source-hero p { font-size: 0.98rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #94a3b8; max-width: 720px; margin-bottom: 28px; }
.source-types {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(160px, 1fr));
    gap: 22px 32px;
}
.source-types div { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; }
.source-types strong { color: #a7f3d0; font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 600; }
.source-types span { color: #64748b; font-size: 0.82rem; }

.reading-strip {
    margin-top: 44px;
    overflow: hidden;
    position: relative;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(148,163,184,0.12);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(148,163,184,0.12);
    padding: 18px 0;
}
.reading-track {
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: 44px;
    white-space: nowrap;
    animation: readingScroll 60s linear infinite;
    will-change: transform;
}
.reading-item {
    font-family: monospace; font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: #64748b;
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}
.reading-dot {
    display: inline-block; width: 6px; height: 6px;
    margin: 0 10px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: #4ade80;
    box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(74,222,128,0.9);
    animation: readingPulse 2s ease-in-out infinite;
}
@keyframes readingPulse {
    0%,100% { opacity: 0.4; }
    50%     { opacity: 1; }
}
@keyframes readingScroll {
    from { transform: translateX(0); }
    to   { transform: translateX(-50%); }
}
.named-sources { margin-top: 32px; font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #64748b; }

/* ===== unique cards ===== */
.unique-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: 24px; margin-top: 32px;
}
.unique-card {
    padding: 28px 26px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(148,163,184,0.14);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: rgba(15,23,42,0.35);
}
.unique-card .num {
    font-family: monospace; font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em; color: #4ade80; margin-bottom: 12px;
}
.unique-card h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; color: #e2e8f0; margin: 0 0 12px; }
.unique-card p { font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.7; color: #94a3b8; margin-bottom: 16px; }
.unique-card .contrast {
    font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.6; color: #64748b;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(148,163,184,0.1);
    padding-top: 12px;
}
.unique-card .contrast strong { color: #a7f3d0; }

/* ===== responsive ===== */
@media (max-width: 780px) {
    .learn-stage { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 32px; }
    .learn-stage:nth-child(even) { direction: ltr; }
    .vine-nodes { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; }
    .vine { height: 40px; }
    .eco-layer { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 16px; padding: 28px 22px; }
    .eco-body ul { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .equation-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 6px; }
    .equation-note { text-align: left; }
}
</style>
</section>

<section id="learning">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>How it <span class="accent">learns</span></h2>
        <p class="lead">
            Three loops, running continuously. Each one improves the system
            without anyone telling it what to look for.
        </p>

        <div class="learn-flow">

            <!-- Stage 1: DNA scanning -->
<div class="learn-stage">
  <div class="learn-visual">
    <div class="helix-wrap">
      <div class="helix">
        <div class="rung"></div><div class="rung"></div><div class="rung"></div>
        <div class="rung"></div><div class="rung"></div><div class="rung"></div>
        <div class="rung"></div><div class="rung"></div><div class="rung"></div>
        <div class="rung"></div><div class="rung"></div><div class="rung"></div>
        <div class="rung"></div><div class="rung"></div><div class="rung"></div>
        <div class="rung"></div><div class="rung"></div><div class="rung"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="scan-sweep"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="learn-copy">
    <span class="stage-badge">Loop 01</span>
    <h3>Reading <span class="accent">raw sequence</span></h3>
    <p>
      Whole chromosomes go in. The system reads the structure
      hidden inside the sequence — the shape of information
      as it unfolds along the genome.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Ingest</strong> whole chromosomes, unedited</li>
      <li><strong>Read</strong> shape, rhythm, and context along the strand</li>
      <li><strong>Discover</strong> the signatures that separate coding from conserved from regulatory from silent</li>
      <li><strong>Validate</strong> across chromosomes and species</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>


<!-- Stage 2: Growing the graph -->
            <div class="learn-stage reverse">
                <div class="learn-visual">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 400 400" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">
                        <defs>
                            <radialGradient id="graphGlow" cx="50%" cy="50%" r="50%">
                                <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#60a5fa" stop-opacity="0.15"/>
                                <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#60a5fa" stop-opacity="0"/>
                            </radialGradient>
                        </defs>

                        <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="150" fill="url(#graphGlow)"/>

                        <!-- Edges -->
                        <line class="graph-edge" x1="200" y1="200" x2="90" y2="90" stroke="#60a5fa" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                        <line class="graph-edge e2" x1="200" y1="200" x2="310" y2="90" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                        <line class="graph-edge e3" x1="200" y1="200" x2="90" y2="310" stroke="#a7f3d0" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                        <line class="graph-edge e4" x1="200" y1="200" x2="310" y2="310" stroke="#34d399" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                        <line class="graph-edge e5" x1="90" y1="90" x2="310" y2="90" stroke="#60a5fa" stroke-width="1"/>
                        <line class="graph-edge e6" x1="90" y1="310" x2="310" y2="310" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1"/>

                        <!-- Nodes -->
                        <circle class="graph-node" cx="200" cy="200" r="22" fill="#0e1a14" stroke="#a7f3d0" stroke-width="2"/>
                        <text x="200" y="205" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="#a7f3d0" font-weight="bold">core</text>

                        <circle class="graph-node n2" cx="90" cy="90" r="14" fill="#0e1a14" stroke="#60a5fa" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                        <text x="90" y="94" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="9" fill="#60a5fa">gene</text>

                        <circle class="graph-node n3" cx="310" cy="90" r="14" fill="#0e1a14" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                        <text x="310" y="94" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="9" fill="#4ade80">var</text>

                        <circle class="graph-node n4" cx="90" cy="310" r="14" fill="#0e1a14" stroke="#a7f3d0" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                        <text x="90" y="314" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="9" fill="#a7f3d0">dis</text>

                        <circle class="graph-node n5" cx="310" cy="310" r="14" fill="#0e1a14" stroke="#34d399" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                        <text x="310" y="314" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="9" fill="#34d399">cpd</text>

                        <circle class="graph-node n6" cx="200" cy="60" r="11" fill="#0e1a14" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                        <text x="200" y="64" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="8" fill="#4ade80">path</text>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <div class="learn-copy">
                    <span class="stage-badge">Loop 02</span>
                    <h3>Growing the <span class="accent">knowledge graph</span></h3>
                    <p>
                        Every new finding becomes a new edge. Variants link to
                        genes. Genes link to pathways. Pathways link to
                        diseases. Diseases link to compounds. The graph grows
                        with every paper published.
                    </p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Ingest</strong> mappings, bindings, structures</li>
                        <li><strong>Connect</strong> variant → gene → disease → compound</li>
                        <li><strong>Query</strong> score candidates, rank outcomes</li>
                        <li><strong>Retrain</strong> new pairs improve predictions</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Stage 3: Continuous loop -->
            <div class="learn-stage">
                <div class="learn-visual">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 400 400" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">
                        <defs>
                            <radialGradient id="cycleGlow" cx="50%" cy="50%" r="50%">
                                <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#a7f3d0" stop-opacity="0.15"/>
                                <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#a7f3d0" stop-opacity="0"/>
                            </radialGradient>
                        </defs>

                        <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="150" fill="url(#cycleGlow)"/>

                        <!-- Outer rotating arc -->
                        <g class="cycle-ring r1">
                            <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="140" fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="60 340" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.5"/>
                        </g>

                        <!-- Middle rotating arc -->
                        <g class="cycle-ring r2">
                            <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="110" fill="none" stroke="#60a5fa" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="50 260" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.6"/>
                        </g>

                        <!-- Inner rotating arc -->
                        <g class="cycle-ring r3">
                            <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="80" fill="none" stroke="#a7f3d0" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="40 160" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.7"/>
                        </g>

                        <!-- Central pulse -->
                        <circle class="pulse-center" cx="200" cy="200" r="45" fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.6"/>
                        <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="28" fill="#040a07" stroke="#a7f3d0" stroke-width="2"/>
                        <text x="200" y="206" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="#a7f3d0" font-weight="bold">loop</text>

                        <!-- Rotating outer labels -->
                        <text x="200" y="45" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="10" fill="#4ade80" opacity="0.7">new evidence</text>
                        <text x="370" y="205" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="10" fill="#60a5fa" opacity="0.7">fetch</text>
                        <text x="200" y="370" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="10" fill="#a7f3d0" opacity="0.7">retrain</text>
                        <text x="30" y="205" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="10" fill="#34d399" opacity="0.7">measure</text>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <div class="learn-copy">
                    <span class="stage-badge">Loop 03</span>
                    <h3>The <span class="accent">continuous cycle</span></h3>
                    <p>
                        Every prediction produces new data, and new data updates
                        the model. If a new feature helps, the classifier keeps
                        it. If it doesn't, the weight fades. Nothing is set in
                        stone.
                    </p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>New evidence</strong> variant, paper, structure</li>
                        <li><strong>Context fetched</strong> class, conservation, motif</li>
                        <li><strong>Model retrains</strong> weights adjust on new inputs</li>
                        <li><strong>Impact measured</strong> help stays, noise fades</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="pipeline">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>The <span class="accent">pipeline</span></h2>
        <p class="lead">From raw genome to treatment protocol — one continuous line.</p>

        <div class="vine-wrap">
            <svg class="vine" viewBox="0 0 1200 120" preserveAspectRatio="none">
                <defs>
                    <linearGradient id="vineGrad" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="100%" y2="0%">
                        <stop offset="0%"  stop-color="#4ade80" stop-opacity="0.05"/>
                        <stop offset="50%" stop-color="#4ade80" stop-opacity="0.75"/>
                        <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#4ade80" stop-opacity="0.05"/>
                    </linearGradient>
                    <radialGradient id="seedGlow" cx="50%" cy="50%" r="50%">
                        <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#4ade80" stop-opacity="0.9"/>
                        <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#4ade80" stop-opacity="0"/>
                    </radialGradient>
                </defs>

                <!-- main vine -->
                <path d="M0,60 C200,20 400,100 600,60 S1000,20 1200,60"
                      fill="none" stroke="url(#vineGrad)" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>

                <!-- secondary tendrils -->
                <path d="M0,60 C200,80 400,20 600,60 S1000,100 1200,60"
                      fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="0.6" opacity="0.18"/>

                <!-- traveling pulse -->
                <circle r="7" fill="url(#seedGlow)">
                    <animateMotion dur="11s" repeatCount="indefinite"
                        path="M0,60 C200,20 400,100 600,60 S1000,20 1200,60"/>
                </circle>

                <!-- seeds -->
                <g>
                    <circle cx="120"  cy="52" r="4" fill="#4ade80"/>
                    <circle cx="360"  cy="72" r="4" fill="#4ade80"/>
                    <circle cx="600"  cy="60" r="4" fill="#4ade80"/>
                    <circle cx="840"  cy="50" r="4" fill="#4ade80"/>
                    <circle cx="1080" cy="62" r="4" fill="#4ade80"/>
                </g>
            </svg>

            <div class="vine-nodes">
                <div class="vine-node">
                    <div class="vn-num">01</div>
                    <div class="vn-title">Read</div>
                    <div class="vn-desc">Classify every window by structural signature.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="vine-node">
                    <div class="vn-num">02</div>
                    <div class="vn-title">Map</div>
                    <div class="vn-desc">Place variation in gene, pathway, evidence.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="vine-node">
                    <div class="vn-num">03</div>
                    <div class="vn-title">Screen</div>
                    <div class="vn-desc">Rank compound libraries by binding potential.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="vine-node">
                    <div class="vn-num">04</div>
                    <div class="vn-title">Score</div>
                    <div class="vn-desc">Combine physical, chemical, contextual signals.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="vine-node">
                    <div class="vn-num">05</div>
                    <div class="vn-title">Design</div>
                    <div class="vn-desc">Multi-compound protocol, one ranking, one plan.</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sample-out">
            <div class="sample-label">sample output — ranked protocol</div>
            <table class="sample-table">
                <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Compound</th><th>Binding</th><th>Evidence</th><th>Confidence</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>1</td><td>resveratrol</td><td>−8.72</td><td>in silico · in vitro · in vivo</td><td>high</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>2</td><td>curcumin</td><td>−7.91</td><td>in silico · in vitro</td><td>high</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>3</td><td>fisetin</td><td>−7.45</td><td>in silico · in vitro · in vivo</td><td>high</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>4</td><td>berberine</td><td>−6.83</td><td>in silico · in vitro</td><td>medium</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>5</td><td>quercetin</td><td>−6.52</td><td>in silico only</td><td>medium</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p class="sample-foot">→ next: combine top 3 into a protocol, simulate outcomes at 30 / 90 / 180 / 365 days, generate full evidence report.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    
</section>

<section id="math">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>The math <span class="accent">underneath</span></h2>
        <p class="lead">
            Sequence is raw potential. Meaning emerges only when a pattern
            is applied in a context. We wrote the math that reads both —
            not assembled from other people's tools, but derived from the
            structure of the genome itself.
        </p>
        <div class="math-narrative">
            <h3>Boundaries are <span class="accent">where biology shifts</span></h3>
            <p>
                The genome isn't uniform. Composition drifts, structure loosens,
                conservation fades. A boundary is placed wherever those shifts
                align — and the same logic runs at three scales at once.
            </p>
            <div class="equation-stack">
                <div class="equation-row">
                    <div class="equation-label">FINE</div>
                    <div class="equation-body">Δ&thinsp;GC &gt; τ<sub>fine</sub> &nbsp;∧&nbsp; Δ&thinsp;H4 &gt; τ<sub>fine</sub></div>
                    <div class="equation-note">local composition shift</div>
                </div>
                <div class="equation-row">
                    <div class="equation-label">MEDIUM</div>
                    <div class="equation-body">∇&thinsp;CpG<sub>O/E</sub> &gt; τ<sub>mid</sub></div>
                    <div class="equation-note">island-scale structure change</div>
                </div>
                <div class="equation-row">
                    <div class="equation-label">COARSE</div>
                    <div class="equation-body">Δ&thinsp;PhyloP &gt; τ<sub>coarse</sub></div>
                    <div class="equation-note">evolutionary signal break</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <h3>Every segment earns a <span class="accent">signature</span></h3>
            <p>
                Between boundaries, each region is described not by a label but
                by a fingerprint — its composition, its reading frame, its skew,
                its conservation across deep time. The classifier is not told
                what to look for. It discovers which combinations of features
                separate one kind of region from another, and holds that
                separation across chromosomes and species.
            </p>
            <div class="feature-ribbon">
                <span>Composition</span><span>Structure</span><span>Frame</span>
                <span>Skew</span><span>Conservation</span><span>Context</span>
            </div>
            <p class="math-close">
                The math is not assembled from other people's tools. Boundary
                detection, feature extraction, and the classifier that reads them
                were all derived from the structure of the genome itself — because
                the genome does not care which library you imported. It only cares
                whether the math is right. This is the part that cannot be
                swapped out for a different package.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
    
</section>

<section id="evidence">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>Evidence across <span class="accent">every layer</span></h2>
        <p class="lead">
            Predictions are checked against three independent kinds of
            evidence — computational, cellular, physiological. A claim
            that survives all three is worth acting on.
        </p>

        <div class="eco-layers">

            <div class="eco-layer">
                <div class="eco-glow eco-glow-green"></div>
                <div class="eco-icon">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" width="56" height="56" fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.3">
                        <circle cx="32" cy="32" r="22" opacity="0.25"/>
                        <circle cx="32" cy="32" r="14" opacity="0.5"/>
                        <circle cx="32" cy="32" r="6" fill="#4ade80" stroke="none" opacity="0.85"/>
                        <circle cx="32" cy="32" r="24" stroke-dasharray="2 6" opacity="0.35">
                            <animateTransform attributeName="transform" type="rotate"
                                from="0 32 32" to="360 32 32" dur="28s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
                        </circle>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <div class="eco-body">
                    <span class="eco-tag">In silico</span>
                    <h3>Computational</h3>
                    <p>Every prediction is stress-tested in pure computation before anything touches a cell. Confidence is estimated from the spread of agreement across independent methods.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Structure prediction</strong> — modeled protein geometry</li>
                        <li><strong>Binding simulation</strong> — strength across methods</li>
                        <li><strong>Cross-validation</strong> — held-out data</li>
                        <li><strong>Confidence intervals</strong> — agreement across approaches</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="eco-layer">
                <div class="eco-glow eco-glow-blue"></div>
                <div class="eco-icon">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" width="56" height="56" fill="none" stroke="#60a5fa" stroke-width="1.3">
                        <circle cx="32" cy="32" r="22" opacity="0.25"/>
                        <circle cx="32" cy="32" r="9" fill="#60a5fa" stroke="none" opacity="0.35"/>
                        <circle cx="24" cy="24" r="2.4" fill="#60a5fa" stroke="none">
                            <animate attributeName="opacity" values="0.4;1;0.4" dur="4s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
                        </circle>
                        <circle cx="40" cy="30" r="2.4" fill="#60a5fa" stroke="none">
                            <animate attributeName="opacity" values="0.4;1;0.4" dur="4s" begin="1s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
                        </circle>
                        <circle cx="30" cy="42" r="2" fill="#60a5fa" stroke="none">
                            <animate attributeName="opacity" values="0.4;1;0.4" dur="4s" begin="2s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
                        </circle>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <div class="eco-body">
                    <span class="eco-tag">In vitro</span>
                    <h3>Cellular</h3>
                    <p>Predictions are compared against real cell-based assays from public literature. Pathway activity, gene expression, and cytotoxicity all feed back into the model.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Cell-line assays</strong> — published screens</li>
                        <li><strong>Pathway response</strong> — signaling under treatment</li>
                        <li><strong>Gene expression</strong> — transcript-level confirmation</li>
                        <li><strong>Cytotoxicity profiles</strong> — safe dose ranges</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="eco-layer">
                <div class="eco-glow eco-glow-mint"></div>
                <div class="eco-icon">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" width="56" height="56" fill="none" stroke="#a7f3d0" stroke-width="1.3">
                        <path d="M14,42 Q18,22 32,26 Q44,18 52,26 Q58,34 50,44 Q40,50 32,46 Q22,50 14,42 Z" opacity="0.9"/>
                        <circle cx="26" cy="32" r="1.8" fill="#a7f3d0" stroke="none"/>
                        <path d="M20,50 Q32,54 44,50" opacity="0.5"/>
                        <path d="M20,50 Q32,54 44,50" opacity="0.3">
                            <animate attributeName="opacity" values="0.3;0.6;0.3" dur="5s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
                        </path>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <div class="eco-body">
                    <span class="eco-tag">In vivo</span>
                    <h3>Physiological</h3>
                    <p>Protocols are evaluated against animal model studies and human trial data. Where the model predicts an outcome, that outcome is checked against published physiological responses.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Animal disease models</strong> — established systems</li>
                        <li><strong>Clinical trial data</strong> — dosing, outcomes, events</li>
                        <li><strong>Human cohorts</strong> — time-to-response</li>
                        <li><strong>Longitudinal outcomes</strong> — durability at follow-up</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>

        <div class="cross-cut">
            <h3>Cross-cutting validation</h3>
            <div class="cross-grid">
                <div><strong>Cross-species</strong><span>Patterns that hold across evolutionary distance.</span></div>
                <div><strong>Animal models</strong><span>Checked against real physiological responses.</span></div>
                <div><strong>Human trial models</strong><span>Evaluated against clinical data.</span></div>
                <div><strong>Held-out evaluation</strong><span>Tested on data never seen during training.</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    
</section>

<section id="sources">


<div class="container">
<div class="src-wrap">
    <h2>It reads the <span class="accent">open web</span></h2>
    <p class="lead">
        The system doesn't wait for someone to hand it data. It reads
        hundreds of curated, reputable URLs — peer-reviewed literature,
        reference genomes, protein structures, clinical registries —
        and grows as new findings are published.
    </p>

    <div class="src-hero">
        <div class="src-kicker">Hundreds of curated sources</div>
        <h3>Reputable <span class="accent">URLs</span>, continuously read</h3>
        <p>
            Peer-reviewed publications, national reference databases,
            protein structure archives, clinical trial registries. Each
            source is vetted. Each new finding updates the graph.
        </p>
        <div class="src-types">
            <div><strong>Publications</strong><span>Peer-reviewed findings</span></div>
            <div><strong>Genomes</strong><span>Reference assemblies</span></div>
            <div><strong>Proteins</strong><span>Structures and functions</span></div>
            <div><strong>Variants</strong><span>Population and clinical</span></div>
            <div><strong>Compounds</strong><span>Bioactivity and libraries</span></div>
            <div><strong>Trials</strong><span>Clinical registries</span></div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="strip-outer">
        <div class="strip-inner">
